    "# SLM Recursive Latent Reasoner: Multi-Seed Falsification Suite\n",
    "\n",
    "An end-to-end, audit-oriented notebook for testing a small language model with recurrent latent computation on synthetic function composition. It upgrades the single-run prototype with independent training seeds, depth-versus-compute interventions, adaptive-halting diagnostics, separately trained baselines, held-out representation formats, intermediate-state probes, raw per-example records, confidence intervals, and checksumed artifacts.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Research question\n",
    "\n",
    "Does a shared recurrent latent transition learn an iterative mechanism that improves depth generalization more reliably than matched non-recurrent and recurrent alternatives on a controlled composition benchmark?\n",
    "\n",
    "## What this study can establish\n",
    "\n",
    "- Whether results reproduce across independent model initialization and data-order seeds.\n",
    "- Whether accuracy depends systematically on permitted latent-loop computation.\n",
    "- Whether recurrent latent states linearly decode independently generated oracle intermediate values.\n",
    "- Whether a shared recurrent transition compares favorably with specified matched baselines on this benchmark.\n",
    "\n",
    "## What it cannot establish\n",
    "\n",
    "It does not demonstrate general intelligence, broad language reasoning, or real-world planning. It evaluates a learned model on a synthetic, executable task. Run every cell in a fresh runtime; retain generated files unchanged after execution."
   ]
  },
